{
  "analysis": "The reference files are being truncated. I can see the communication protocol structure - each agent needs SKILL.md, inbox/, outbox/, workspace/, and status.json. I need to read the full sub-agent-templates.md to understand the templates for creating agents.",
  "plan": "Read the full content of sub-agent-templates.md and communication-protocol.md using head/tail or less to see all the details, then create the 4-agent pipeline.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -150 skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the agent framework. Each agent needs a workspace with SKILL.md, inbox/, outbox/, workspace/, and status.json. The agents communicate via files - each agent reads from its inbox and writes to its outbox. The pipeline flow is: data-collector → analyst → writer → reviewer, with final output going to final_output/.",
  "plan": "Create the 4-agent pipeline structure. I'll create directories for each agent with their SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, status.json, outbox/, and workspace/. Then I'll wire up the dependencies and run each agent in sequence.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p agents/{data-collector,analyst,writer,reviewer}/{inbox,outbox,workspace}\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la agents/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

